input.body:
The sheepdog pack's reports each lose repos depending on their state, so no single report accounts for the whole fleet:

- the **census** summary names uncovered/opted-out/skipped repos but only *counts* covered members, and says nothing about dormancy;
- the **freshness** sweep names unhealthy and dormant members but only counts fresh ones and lumps archived/fork/excluded/uncovered into an opaque "out of scope" count;
- **fleet-usage** silently skips uncovered and archived/fork/excluded repos entirely, and never says which folding members had no captured activity that day;
- **force-baseline** silently skips canon, archived/fork/excluded, filter misses, and uncovered repos.

The sheepdog should provide data on the fleet regardless of state: if a repo is not in Claudinite, say so; if it's dormant, say so; if it was inactive today, say so. Every report should land each repo under exactly one named state — a roster that names only the exceptions has silent holes, and a reader cannot tell "fine" from "fell out of the report".

